WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:03.373
So, what do you want?

00:03.542 --> 00:06.670
Nachos, Red Hots, Milk Duds,
popcorn and a Slushee.

00:07.112 --> 00:10.240
What are you doing?
Building an ass bomb?

00:10.982 --> 00:12.882
- Pick two.
- Okay.

00:13.051 --> 00:14.643
- Popcorn and Milk Duds.
- Fine.

00:14.820 --> 00:16.811
- Large popcorn.
- Okay.

00:16.988 --> 00:20.389
But I'll still need a Slushee
so I don't choke to death on a Milk Dud.

00:20.959 --> 00:23.223
- All right.
- And ask them to pump nacho cheese...

00:23.395 --> 00:24.987
...on the popcorn.

00:25.363 --> 00:27.695
Oh, that reminds me.
I got a date tonight.

00:27.866 --> 00:29.834
That reminds you?

00:30.202 --> 00:31.829
Yeah, and I'm gonna need your help.

00:32.003 --> 00:33.834
- My help?
Next.

00:34.005 --> 00:35.233
Hang on.

00:35.407 --> 00:37.841
A large popcorn with cheese...

00:38.009 --> 00:40.842
...a large Slushee
and a jumbo box of Milk Duds.

00:41.012 --> 00:42.843
- You want anything? My treat.
- I'm okay.

00:43.014 --> 00:45.539
I'll just eat whatever lands
on the kid's shirt.

00:45.717 --> 00:46.911
You're gonna go hungry.

00:48.620 --> 00:49.746
That's it.

00:49.921 --> 00:51.582
So, what about this date?

00:51.757 --> 00:54.624
She's got a friend visiting
from out of town, and I said fine.

00:54.793 --> 00:57.193
You know, two's company,
three's a sandwich.

00:57.362 --> 01:00.559
But for some reason she insists
on the friend having her own date.

01:00.732 --> 01:02.859
- So you're asking me?
- Yeah.

01:03.034 --> 01:06.060
The two of us out making the scene
with a couple of hot chicks?

01:06.238 --> 01:08.103
Oh, Lord, never mind.

01:08.273 --> 01:10.537
Don't be silly, it'll be fun.
We never double.

01:10.709 --> 01:13.610
- That's not an accident, Alan.
- Come on. Please, please, please?

01:13.779 --> 01:16.771
- All right, save your begging for the date.
- I never beg.

01:17.282 --> 01:19.113
I grovel.

01:19.518 --> 01:21.782
I guess I'll have to find a babysitter
for Jake.

01:21.953 --> 01:24.786
I don't need a babysitter.
Nothing's gonna happen to me.

01:24.956 --> 01:27.083
Worried about you?
I'm worried about my house.

01:27.259 --> 01:28.385
That's $24.50.

01:28.994 --> 01:30.962
Whoa. Okay.

01:31.696 --> 01:33.561
Oh, jeez.

01:34.132 --> 01:35.929
- What?
- I walked out of the house...

01:36.101 --> 01:38.228
...without my wallet. Can you believe it?

01:38.403 --> 01:40.496
Strangely enough, I can.

01:40.672 --> 01:43.197
- Twenty-four-fifty, please.
- Hang on.

01:43.375 --> 01:47.402
I know what happened. Because you drove,
it didn't occur to me to pick up my wallet.

01:47.579 --> 01:51.948
The only reason I drove is because
you said your car was low on gas.

01:52.117 --> 01:54.312
Twenty-four-fifty, please.

01:54.486 --> 01:56.681
Just a minute.
You said you'd pay for parking...

01:56.855 --> 01:59.847
...which you won't be able to do
because you "forgot" your wallet.

02:00.025 --> 02:01.925
Don't make a big deal,
I'll pay next time.

02:02.093 --> 02:05.426
- That's what you said last time.
- Yes, but this time I forgot my wallet.

02:05.597 --> 02:08.862
Twenty-four-fifty, please!

02:11.369 --> 02:13.667
Fine, I'll pay.

02:14.372 --> 02:17.864
You know what, why don't you throw
in a bagel dog, make it an even 30.

02:45.604 --> 02:48.937
Okay. Uncle Charlie and I
are leaving now.

02:49.107 --> 02:51.439
- Bye.
- I'm trusting you to act responsibly...

02:51.610 --> 02:55.171
...and go to bed at a reasonable hour.
- Okay.

02:56.081 --> 02:58.481
You know, this is
a real turning point for you.

02:59.217 --> 03:02.584
You're taking care of yourself.
You're becoming a man.

03:02.754 --> 03:04.619
You too.

03:06.958 --> 03:10.758
Boy, it seems like only yesterday that
I was bringing you home from the hospital.

03:10.929 --> 03:13.864
You were... You were like
a little wrinkly pig with colic.

03:15.133 --> 03:16.930
Yeah, are you going or not?

03:19.004 --> 03:20.801
- Are you ready?
- Hang on.

03:23.108 --> 03:24.939
Goodbye, my son.

03:25.944 --> 03:28.572
Save it for the date, Dad.

03:32.918 --> 03:36.854
Don't burn the place down, and if you do,
don't be here when I get back.

03:38.723 --> 03:42.181
He knows to drink the cheap Scotch,
not the single malt, right?

03:43.028 --> 03:44.427
- Not funny.
- I'm not joking.

03:44.596 --> 03:47.463
He's probably just gonna mix it
with Hawaiian Punch anyway.

03:51.836 --> 03:53.167
Oh, God, I am so full.

03:53.338 --> 03:56.205
I don't think I could put another thing
in my mouth.

03:56.374 --> 03:59.207
I hope that's just a figure of speech.

04:01.479 --> 04:03.811
This is such a beautiful restaurant.

04:03.982 --> 04:06.041
They don't have anything like this
back home.

04:06.217 --> 04:08.515
Really? They don't have nice restaurants
in Idaho?

04:08.687 --> 04:12.020
Oh, well, yeah. I mean, we have
a T.G.I. Friday's and an Applebee's...

04:12.190 --> 04:15.023
...but you never see movie stars
like we did here.

04:15.627 --> 04:17.686
Nina, they're just regular people.

04:17.862 --> 04:21.195
And technically, I wouldn't call
Geraldo Rivera a movie star.

04:22.801 --> 04:24.598
Well, I thought it was very exciting.

04:24.769 --> 04:26.669
Since I'm only in town for the weekend...

04:26.838 --> 04:29.898
...I think we should go
absolutely crazy tonight.

04:32.243 --> 04:33.938
Is it too late to switch dates?

04:34.713 --> 04:36.180
I'm up for that.

04:36.348 --> 04:39.044
- No kidding.
- As long as we can switch back.

04:39.217 --> 04:41.208
Alan, I believe it's time
we get the check.

04:42.387 --> 04:44.355
- Agreed.
- Check, please.

04:44.522 --> 04:46.456
- Be right back.
- Where you going?

04:46.624 --> 04:47.682
The little boys' room.

04:48.360 --> 04:50.794
He means the little cheap
bastards' room.

04:51.229 --> 04:55.029
- What's that, Charlie?
- Nothing. Excuse me.

04:56.101 --> 04:58.934
Back home we just call it the crapper.

05:21.559 --> 05:24.187
I thought you had to pee.

05:24.596 --> 05:26.860
I did. I do. I am.

05:53.291 --> 05:57.694
- Nice girls.
- Yeah, they're terrific.

06:31.563 --> 06:35.659
No matter how you shake and dance,
the last few drops fall on your pants.

06:41.005 --> 06:43.599
Maybe you shouldn't wear khakis.

07:03.461 --> 07:05.156
Uh-oh.

07:09.200 --> 07:11.498
- What are you doing?
- What do you think I'm doing?

07:13.104 --> 07:15.129
Amazing.

07:15.773 --> 07:18.173
This might take a while, Charlie.

07:19.043 --> 07:21.568
All right, let's play.

07:27.252 --> 07:30.915
What are you doing?
What do you think I'm doing?

07:31.089 --> 07:33.182
Okay. Okay.

07:33.725 --> 07:36.193
Hey, Alan?
Yeah?

07:36.361 --> 07:38.659
This might take a while.

07:42.100 --> 07:43.226
&lt;i>MAN
Where's Jennifer?&lt;/i>

07:43.401 --> 07:45.130
&lt;i>WoMAN:
She went into the caretaker's shack...&lt;/i>

07:45.303 --> 07:46.395
&lt;i>...to look for Corey.&lt;/i>

07:46.571 --> 07:50.473
&lt;i>Okay, you stay here. I'll go find her.
WoMAN: No, I'm coming with you.&lt;/i>

07:50.642 --> 07:54.100
Will you people quit going
into the caretaker's shack?

07:56.481 --> 07:58.972
&lt;i>WoMAN:
Corey? Are you in here?&lt;/i>

07:59.150 --> 08:02.586
No, you idiot.
Corey's been dead for an hour.

08:03.621 --> 08:04.952
&lt;i>Corey?&lt;/i>

08:08.393 --> 08:11.055
Man, I should have went to bed.

08:28.079 --> 08:29.137
Are you crazy?

08:29.314 --> 08:32.647
Well, there are several
schools of thought on that.

08:32.817 --> 08:34.944
So your dad let you stay
by yourself tonight.

08:35.119 --> 08:37.519
Why not? I'm old enough.
I don't need a babysitter.

08:37.689 --> 08:40.180
Okay.
Well, then I'll leave you to your movie.

08:41.693 --> 08:45.629
Wait, wait, you don't have to go.
Want a Pop-Tart?

08:46.864 --> 08:47.990
Sure, why not?

08:49.634 --> 08:51.932
So, what do I need to know?

08:52.103 --> 08:56.472
Well, basically, when a guy
has half a face, you leave him alone.

09:01.746 --> 09:07.082
Charlie, you still there?
I told you it might take a while.

09:08.353 --> 09:13.120
Well, I guess this train isn't ready
to leave the station.

09:18.863 --> 09:22.196
You know what they say, better
to be on the toilet and not have to go...

09:22.367 --> 09:25.336
...than to have to go
and not be on the toilet.

09:26.237 --> 09:28.501
Really? And who says that?

09:29.207 --> 09:32.802
I don't know. It's folk wisdom.

09:57.402 --> 10:00.701
The liquid soap is a nice idea
for the house, don't you think?

10:02.040 --> 10:03.234
I guess.

10:03.408 --> 10:07.003
Makes sense when you think about it.
You wash your hands with a bar of soap...

10:07.178 --> 10:09.669
...you're passing your germs on
to the next guy...

10:11.115 --> 10:14.107
...but with the liquid soap,
it's not an issue.

10:18.756 --> 10:20.485
Good idea.

10:21.359 --> 10:24.089
I'll tell Berta to pick up
some liquid soap.

10:25.163 --> 10:27.393
Great. Great.

10:32.737 --> 10:34.967
How funny is Berta?

10:37.241 --> 10:38.538
She is a pistol.

11:09.374 --> 11:11.865
Don't wanna get athlete's hand.

11:37.902 --> 11:40.097
Another good idea for the house.

11:45.009 --> 11:46.169
Uh-oh.

11:46.344 --> 11:48.335
Don't even think about it.

11:49.947 --> 11:53.178
- Where'd they go?
- Your lady friends left 20 minutes ago.

11:53.551 --> 11:57.419
- What? Why?
- Said something about life being too short.

11:57.955 --> 11:59.980
Are you happy?

12:00.625 --> 12:03.685
All right, just give me the check.
Which you and I will split.

12:03.861 --> 12:07.388
Not necessary. Mr. Rivera took care of it
before he left with the ladies.

12:07.865 --> 12:10.800
I guess they'll find out
how at large he really is.

12:12.270 --> 12:15.569
- Unbelievable.
- I know.

12:15.740 --> 12:17.731
We got a free dinner.

12:31.022 --> 12:34.458
Boy, college students are really stupid.

12:37.395 --> 12:39.420
Yeah, if you shouldn't run
with scissors...

12:39.597 --> 12:42.828
...you definitely shouldn't run
with hedge clippers.

12:44.402 --> 12:46.700
I can't believe I missed out
on a sure thing...

12:46.871 --> 12:50.170
...because I was sitting on the can
listening to you not take a crap.

12:50.341 --> 12:52.400
Blaming me because I had
to go to the bathroom?

12:52.577 --> 12:55.512
You didn't have to,
you were trying to stick me with the check.

12:55.847 --> 12:58.714
Oh, I see. So you know my bowels
better than I do?

12:58.883 --> 13:02.216
I will when I pull them out
through your nostrils.

13:04.489 --> 13:06.116
I don't have to listen to this.

13:06.290 --> 13:08.349
What's your hurry?
You see a check coming?

13:12.029 --> 13:14.759
What do you think?
Should we watch the rest of the movie?

13:14.932 --> 13:18.390
Might as well.
I'm not gonna sleep tonight anyway.

13:19.804 --> 13:21.863
- Leave me alone, Charlie.
- No, no, no. No.

13:22.039 --> 13:23.597
Let's get this out in the open.

13:23.774 --> 13:26.470
There's nothing to get out.
I had to go to the bathroom.

13:26.644 --> 13:29.943
Even though I don't have much money,
I was prepared to split the check.

13:30.114 --> 13:31.877
Not fifty-fifty,
you had better wine...

13:32.049 --> 13:35.109
...and your date had two appetizers,
but my fair share.

13:35.753 --> 13:38.051
- What are you doing?
- What do you think?

13:38.222 --> 13:41.419
Alan, you can sit but you can't hide.

13:42.627 --> 13:45.118
I'm going to shower
and get ready for bed.

13:46.030 --> 13:48.157
You're kidding.
You're gonna walk away from me?

13:48.332 --> 13:51.392
Well, Charlie, when you're being irrational
you leave me no choice.

13:51.569 --> 13:53.730
I'm not being irrational.

13:55.907 --> 13:59.070
You wanna see irrational?
Here's irrational.

14:10.054 --> 14:11.078
Oh, great.

14:12.023 --> 14:13.888
My lamp.

14:18.863 --> 14:20.160
What the hell?

14:30.308 --> 14:32.674
I don't freaking believe it.

15:02.473 --> 15:05.374
Charlie, the pizza's here.

15:10.214 --> 15:11.875
So it is.

15:16.287 --> 15:21.384
- Hey, why don't I get this one?
- Hey, why don't you?

15:25.229 --> 15:27.322
What? No wallet?

15:28.633 --> 15:30.658
- I'll be right back.
- I'll wait.

15:41.045 --> 15:45.448
- There you go, Mr. Harper, 22.75.
- Thanks, Gordon. Hang on.

15:56.427 --> 15:58.292
Keep the change.

15:58.462 --> 16:01.761
- Wow. Thanks.
- Oh, Gordon, wait, wait, wait.

16:01.932 --> 16:04.093
- You gotta hear something.
- Hear what?

16:04.268 --> 16:06.133
Shh.

16:07.004 --> 16:08.699
Wait for it.

16:13.544 --> 16:18.743
- Was that it?
- Yep. Thanks for waiting.

16:33.564 --> 16:34.826
Looking for something?

16:34.999 --> 16:36.694
Yeah, my...

16:36.867 --> 16:38.334
...wallet.

16:41.639 --> 16:43.402
Here it is.

16:44.508 --> 16:47.477
- Oh. Oh, thanks.
- Wow.

16:47.645 --> 16:50.944
The legendary lost wallet of Alan Harper.

16:52.349 --> 16:53.407
Funny.

17:03.327 --> 17:05.921
Oh, my, there's no money in here.

17:06.530 --> 17:08.998
- No?
- No.

17:09.166 --> 17:11.532
How were you gonna pay
for the pizza, Alan?

17:11.702 --> 17:14.170
I have, um...

17:14.338 --> 17:16.363
- I have...
- What is it, Alan?

17:16.540 --> 17:18.303
What do you have?

17:20.211 --> 17:22.509
- Nothing.
- You sure?

17:23.247 --> 17:26.182
Oh, where did you find that?
I mean, what is that?

17:27.151 --> 17:29.381
About $5000 in small bills.

17:30.020 --> 17:31.988
Wow, that much?

17:32.156 --> 17:34.818
A little less, since I paid for the pizza.

17:34.992 --> 17:36.619
And tipped the guy a 50.

17:36.794 --> 17:39.888
- You gave him a $50 tip?
- Yep.

17:40.064 --> 17:43.192
Now I'm gonna go light my cigar
with a hundred.

17:43.434 --> 17:45.334
Wait, wait, wait.
Wait, wait, wait.

17:45.503 --> 17:50.372
I just remembered. I lost a big roll of bills
that looked a lot like that one.

17:51.008 --> 17:54.205
Really? It's yours? I had no idea.

17:54.979 --> 17:57.072
An honest mistake. Give me.

17:57.348 --> 17:58.906
You can understand my confusion.

17:59.083 --> 18:02.143
A guy's got this kind of cash,
you'd think he'd be able to pay...

18:02.319 --> 18:04.150
...for his own freaking bagel dog.

18:05.055 --> 18:07.523
You don't understand.
The money isn't for me.

18:08.092 --> 18:10.219
Really? Who's it for?

18:11.328 --> 18:12.818
Old Alan.

18:13.330 --> 18:17.664
- Old Alan?
- Yeah. You know, the Alan of the future.

18:18.235 --> 18:21.204
You're kidding. They're still gonna have
Alans in the future?

18:21.872 --> 18:26.571
No, see, the thing is, I've been going
through a kind of a rough financial time...

18:26.744 --> 18:30.840
...since, well, high school.

18:31.048 --> 18:34.950
It occurred to me that I could wind up
an old man with no one to take care of me.

18:35.119 --> 18:37.849
I mean, who will old Alan
be able to count on?

18:38.022 --> 18:41.924
Certainly not Jake, because let's face it,
his best hope of a steady income...

18:42.092 --> 18:44.925
...is if missing the toilet
becomes a professional sport.

18:47.431 --> 18:51.094
So I decided that whenever somebody
in the office paid in cash...

18:51.268 --> 18:54.601
...I'd put it away for old Alan.

18:55.472 --> 18:58.873
- What about the IRS?
- Them? They don't care about old Alan.

19:00.377 --> 19:02.971
Okay, let me get this straight.

19:03.147 --> 19:05.479
You're squirreling away money
for old Alan...

19:05.649 --> 19:08.311
...while young Alan sponges off
of dumb Charlie.

19:08.986 --> 19:11.580
I wouldn't call you dumb.
Sweet Charlie, loving Charlie.

19:11.755 --> 19:14.747
- Can I have my money now?
- You have a serious problem, my friend.

19:14.925 --> 19:17.257
Yes, I do. No question.
Now give me my money.

19:18.729 --> 19:21.459
- You need help.
- I know, but who can afford it?

19:24.301 --> 19:27.395
All right. You know what I want you to do
with this money?

19:27.571 --> 19:30.972
Come on, man.
I'm already constipated.

19:31.876 --> 19:34.936
You're gonna spend it. Every penny.

19:35.412 --> 19:39.439
But... But what about old Alan?
What will he do?

19:39.617 --> 19:43.417
Well, I'm guessing old Alan
will be living on old Charlie's hide-a-bed...

19:43.587 --> 19:45.680
...until they bag him and tag him.

19:47.858 --> 19:53.421
Really? You mean no matter what,
I can always count on you?

19:55.733 --> 19:57.598
Keep the money.

20:08.779 --> 20:12.215
There you go. Enjoy your movie.

20:14.818 --> 20:17.946
- Hi, Charlie.
- Hey, bro.

20:18.656 --> 20:20.385
I'll take a big box of Milk Duds.

20:20.557 --> 20:23.822
Sure. That's $25.

20:24.962 --> 20:29.558
- Anything for your lady friend?
- That's okay. She doesn't eat.

20:30.200 --> 20:31.861
Food.

20:32.670 --> 20:35.696
- Keep the change.
- Oh, thanks, Charlie.

20:35.873 --> 20:37.340
I can always count on you.

20:38.242 --> 20:39.903
Come on, baby.

20:41.111 --> 20:43.705
Can you believe I'm older than him?

20:45.749 --> 20:47.876
Boy, that's some hot chick.

20:49.119 --> 20:50.552
Yeah.

20:53.390 --> 20:57.087
- Don't eat the popcorn, Jake.
- Sorry, Dad.
